# entropylab v1.0.0 — release sums, GPG-signed (Bitcoin-style SHA256SUMS.asc)
#
# Source commit attested: c1037ba3a20d0c6db1b3265a7385b2944ce827e6
# (stamped in the page footer; artifact commit 9f72975 on rock carries the
# built artifact, 372a507 its OpenTimestamps proof). v1.0.0 promotes
# v1.0.0rc3 unchanged: same commit, same entropylab.html, same
# SHA256SUMS.txt, so the rc3 signature blocks below cover it as-is.
#
# Every signature block below is a detached signature over the committed
# file SHA256SUMS.txt — nothing else. A committed file is the payload so
# there is exactly one byte sequence to sign.
#
# Verify (one gpg call checks every signer block at once):
#
#     gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS.txt
#     sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS.txt
#
# The WASM module hashes in WASM-SHA256SUMS.txt are covered transitively:
# the modules are inlined into entropylab.html, whose hash SHA256SUMS.txt
# carries.
#
# Layout: one entry per signer — "Signer:"/"Key:" label lines, then the
# armored detached signature block.
#
# Everything outside the PGP armor (this header included) is NOT signed;
# trust only what verifies. Signer public keys are posted with each
# signature in the PR #832 comments: current GnuPG (tested 2.4.8) refuses
# to verify a file that mixes in key blocks or stacked cleartext-signed
# messages ("multiple plaintexts seen"), so this file stacks detached
# signatures, exactly as current Bitcoin Core SHA256SUMS.asc does.
#
# To add your signature: follow the PR #832 description — comment with
# your Key: line, armored public key, and detached signature block; the
# maintainer verifies and appends.
#
